decimal — attribution
====================================================================

This module is MIT (see the repository LICENSE). It contains no third-party
source code and no third-party test data: the test vectors in `src/testdata/`
are generated by `tools/py_conform.py` and `tools/py_oracle.py` from operands
produced by those scripts, with expected values computed by Python's `decimal`
module at generation time.

Design references (published definitions only, no source code consulted or
copied): Java `BigDecimal` / `RoundingMode` javadoc, the IBM General Decimal
Arithmetic specification, and the Python `decimal` documentation. They are
recorded in this module's `README.md` `Provenance:` statement as provenance,
not as a condition.
